    "result_text": "The build is green \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`, all tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nI unified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, and removed the standalone `checkDigit` field.\n\n**Format** (e.g. `NSW2716E6609E1`): REGION (region code from postcode/city) + FY (2-digit fiscal year of the business-day-adjusted registration date) + HASH8 (first 8 upper-hex of SHA-256 over `telephone+lastName`, the same hash the region-and-hash identity uses) + CHK (single Luhn check digit over the digits of `<REGION><FY><HASH8>`).\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 replaced the `customerCode`, `checkDigit`, and `membershipNumber` schema properties with a single `memberId` property (regenerates the DTO).\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 removed the `customerCode`/`membershipNumber` fields, columns, and accessors; added `memberId` (`member_id` column) with getter/setter.\n- **SQL schemas** (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres) \u2014 replaced the `customer_code`/`membership_number` columns with a single `member_id` column.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 replaced `customerCode(...)`/`membershipNumber(...)` with a `memberId(...)` builder that assembles REGION+FY+HASH8+CHK (new `luhnCheckDigit` helper) and applies **collision handling to the memberId** (appending `-<n>` on clash). `primaryIdentifier` now returns the memberId, and the **audit** line and `OwnerCreatedEvent` JSON both carry `memberId`.\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 dropped the `checkDigit` mapping and method; **`locality`** now derives REGION from the memberId (feeding `ownerSegment`), and **`fiscalYear`** now derives FY from the memberId \u2014 each with the seed-data fallback preserved.\n\nThe trailing segments of the memberId are fixed-width (FY=2, HASH8=8, CHK=1), so the mapper parses REGION/FY by offset from the end, stripping any `-<n>` collision suffix first.\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreReturnsUnifiedMemberId` test and the full suite pass.",
